A||||7||ur2biteme||well, here's my tranny story.......||||8||
Z||000000||ur2biteme||11-05-2000||05:08 PM||||well, i finally got a little un-intimidated about my tranny problem.  i went out a couple nights ago, fired it up and tried to see where the "grinding" noise was coming from.  well, turns out it's not a grinding noise, but a knocking noise that matches the speed that the clutch is rotating (i put the clutch in, it slows down and stops).  the knocking is coming from where the bellhousings mate up.  if i didn't know better, i'd want to say that a rod was knocking, but after pulling the vss and seeing no oil, i'm sure that's not the case.  there is obviously a blown seal somewhere, either the shaft the clutch bolts to in the tranny (pardon my ignorance), or the axle seal on the passenger side, or both.  i see oil in that area that isnt from my normal oil leak on the pulley side of the engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>everything shifts fine, without the oil, the clutch works properly.  any ideas, let me know.  i'm probably replacing the tranny anyway, i'd just like to figure out for my refrence||||reg||8
Z||000001||Raydar||11-05-2000||06:31 PM||||Almost sounds like the input shaft bearing said adios. That's the shaft that the clutch disk turns. Almost <I>had</I> to take the seal with it, if it went. <BR>When you remove the trans, make sure that the pilot bushing is in place. It's a little bronze bushing in the end of the crankshaft. Helps to support the end of the input shaft.   <BR>I <I>know</I> the pilot bushing thing is true for standard RWD GM manual trannies. I believe that Fieros are the same. I remember reading a post, a few months back, that said that <I>only automatics</I> used a pilot bushing. Made no sense to me. <BR>Can anybody check me on this?<P>Raydar<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||ur2biteme||11-05-2000||06:54 PM||||would that explain the small metal chunks i found around my VSS?  i forgot to mention that.  also too, is the tranny salvagable for less than just replacing it?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||11-05-2000||07:13 PM||||V6's don't have pilot bearings, don't know about the 4||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||11-05-2000||07:59 PM||||None of the Fieros use a pilot bushing for the input shaft. ur2biteme, what type of trans is it? Unless it's a Getrag, it's probably not worth anything anymore, just find another one.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
Z||000005||ur2biteme||11-06-2000||03:24 AM||||it's an isuzu, so i guess my original plan was the best route.  oh well, i'll let them cart the damn thing off then.  lol.  well at any rate, my plan now is to put another isuzu in and see if it lasts 6-9 months for me to gather the stuff to put the M19 in, which i've started lusting over lol. i want the short gears and like the idea of "bulletproof" being the reputation for the tranny that's in my car.  just don't like the idea that the same car company that produced the impulse made my tranny (no flames intended, just prefrence).  i will say that when the damn things work, the shift great.  when they work......   <P>oh well, i'll stop whining.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
Z||000006||fldevel||11-06-2000||12:54 PM||||sounds like your tranny ran outa oil and your syncronizers froze up .. tranny re-build time .. oh and look for cracks in the housing .. i just re-built a tranny to find oil leaking outa a small crack just above the engine mount .. i ended up buying a new tranny anyway ||||reg||1
Z||000007||ur2biteme||11-06-2000||09:14 PM||||well, i'm replacing the tranny, but the oil started leaking out AFTER the knocking started.  the tranny still shifts fine, even without the oil, and with the knock.  oh well, their cheap enough, just wish that i had a place to work on it so i didn't have to pay $300 to put in a $150 part.||||reg||1
